Package: libablemon1.8
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libs
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: maintained fork of LEMON, a C++ library of network optimization
 abLEMON is a maintained fork of LEMON, the Library for Efficient Modeling
 and Optimization in Networks: a C++ template library of graphs, maps and
 heaps and of the algorithms of network optimization built on them
 (shortest paths, maximum and minimum cost flows, matchings, connectivity,
 cuts and cycles), with the certificates of infeasible and unbounded minimum
 cost flow problems and the k best flows. It keeps the headers, the
 namespace and the CMake package of LEMON.
 .
 This package holds the shared library.

Package: ablemon-dev
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libdevel
Depends: libablemon1.8 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Conflicts: liblemon-dev
Replaces: liblemon-dev
Description: maintained fork of LEMON (development files)
 abLEMON is a maintained fork of LEMON, the Library for Efficient Modeling
 and Optimization in Networks: a C++ template library of graphs, maps and
 heaps and of the algorithms of network optimization built on them
 (shortest paths, maximum and minimum cost flows, matchings, connectivity,
 cuts and cycles), with the certificates of infeasible and unbounded minimum
 cost flow problems and the k best flows. It keeps the headers, the
 namespace and the CMake package of LEMON.
 .
 This package holds the headers, the pkg-config file and the CMake
 configuration that find_package(LEMON) finds; it takes the place of
 liblemon-dev, whose headers are installed in the same directory.
